                "lastName": "Schlesinger"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The paper describes an efficient and economic demodulator for intercarrier television sound. The circuit uses the method of sampling near zero passage of the carrier. This is accomplished in one-half of a double triode. The other half operates as a locked oscillator, whose cathode output is used to drive the sampler cathode. The phase angles between grid and cathode of the sampler are not in quadrature. A centering method to obtain coincidence between optimum fm detection and best AM rejection is described.",
